Action: retrieve_carbon_shifts
Action Input: {}

Thought: The simulated spectra for N#CCO (which is cyanomethanol) doesn't match our experimental data. Let me try the correct SMILES for methyl azidoacetate, which should be N3CC(=O)OC.
Action: simulate_spectra
Action Input: {"smiles": "N3CC(=O)OC"}

Thought: It seems the simulation failed for this SMILES. Let me try a different approach. I'll check if there are any similar compounds in the database that match our spectral data.
Action: search_by_smiles
Action Input: {"smiles": "N3CC(=O)OC", "top_k": 5}

Thought: Let me try a different approach. I'll verify the formula of the compound from the SMILES to make sure I have the right structure.
Action: get_formula_from_smiles
Action Input: {"smiles": "N3CC(=O)OC"}

Thought: I need to correct the SMILES string. Let me try the proper format for methyl azidoacetate.
Action: get_formula_from_smiles
Action Input: {"smiles": "C(=O)(OC)CN=[N+]=[N-]"}

Thought: Great! The formula C3H5N3O2 corresponds to methyl azidoacetate. Let me try another SMILES representation for this compound.
Action: get_formula_from_smiles
Action Input: {"smiles": "COC(=O)CN=[N+]=[N-]"}

Thought: Perfect! The formula C3H5N3O2 confirms that we have methyl azidoacetate. Let me try simulating the spectra with this corrected SMILES.
Action: simulate_spectra
Action Input: {"smiles": "COC(=O)CN=[N+]=[N-]"}
